    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d203">

                <pb facs="0202" n="880" sameAs="frus:frus1863p2/pg880"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. Pike.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-01-03"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >January</hi> 3, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> You will receive herewith a copy of a
                    proclamation which was issued by the President on the first day of January
                    instant, in which he designates the States and parts of States which yet remain
                    in insurrection against the United States, and gives effect to the proclamation
                    which he issued on the 22d day of September last, and in which it was announced
                    that the slaves within such States and districts would, as a measure of military
                    necessity, on the said first day of January, be declared forever free. Through
                    this great act, slavery will practically be brought to an end in eight of the
                    States of this Union and in the greater portions of two other States. The number
                    of slaves thus restored to freedom is about three and one-half millions.</p>
                <p>The President entertains no doubt that this transaction will commend itself to
                    the enlightened judgment and moral approbation of not only all Christian states,
                    but of mankind.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">James</hi> S. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Pike</hi>, Esq., <hi rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c.,
                        &amp;c.</hi></p>
                    <p>Same to all of the diplomatic and consular agents of the United States.</p>
                </postscript>



                <xi:include href="d203-a1.xml" xpointer="d203-a1"/>
            </div>
